  "instruments/cert-unit/render.mjs": "the CSS block's literal hex was frontier's palette; three values (#111114, #e8e8ee, #83838f) are on no scale this site owns and check-wiring caught them. Replaced with house tokens, each keeping the original as its var() fallback so the module still draws outside a page that defines them.",
  "instruments/cert-unit/contact.mjs": "two CSS literals were frontier's palette and on no scale this site owns: .cp #5f5f6b -> #6e6e7a (--ink-4), .ct #e8e8ee -> #f6f6f8 (--ink), so the contact sheet passes the palette gate when a page inlines it (2026-09-05)"
 },
 "notPorted": {
  "the marks": "circumplex plate, envelope ruler, contact-sheet glyph, deformation field, ensemble renderer \u2014 designed for their own data; generalising them early makes them worse (operator instruction).",
  "template.js": "cert-machine's design/template.js + nav.js win: they carry the nav, SEO, OG and the gates, and frontier's 72-line shell carries none of that.",
